=====================================================================
BOTTOM LINE for the lead.  Criteria 2, 3 and 5 are proven. Criterion 4 is
proven at uid 1000 and fails at uid 0 on a pre-existing test. Criterion 1 --
the oracle, which the brief makes authoritative -- exits 1 in both
environments, on two checks that reduce to a `-timeout 600s` in F1's and F2's
accept.sh being shorter than this host's 1027s -race runtime. I found no
defect in attempt 4's own change: the two new tests exist, assert their named
properties, and each is the sole test that dies under its own mutation. But I
cannot certify a criterion whose command exits 1, so this is FAIL rather than
PASS-with-caveats. Making it PASSable here needs two things that are the
lead's to authorise, not the worker's: a larger -race timeout in the F1/F2
oracles, and either a non-root grading environment or a root guard on
TestRollbackDecryptionWithRecipientReportsUnrestorableFiles.
